where fL,S(l,s) is the joint probability density function of the load and the structural strength
and Ω is the failure region where SL > SS [37]. Based on this measurement now it would
be possible to make design decisions; for example, to find the most reliable design (i.e. the
design with the lowest probability of failure) or to evaluate the risk associated with a given
design. Note that when the joint probability density function is a multivariate Gaussian
distribution, the probability of failure can be calculated analytically. However, in most cases,
the joint probability density function is not known and it is necessary to resort to numerical
