14 Introduction
an associated uncertainty that needs to be reported. Apart from the technique employed to
solve the model, some other sources of uncertainty lie in the assumptions of the mathematical
model, the initial and boundary conditions, and the model variables. Using computational
methods, these sources of uncertainty can be propagated through the model to obtain the
uncertainty in the responses. The introduction of these methods in engineering design has
allowed to perform different activities, such as uncertainty quantification and sensitivity
analysis, optimisation under uncertainty, and risk analysis.
