3.6.1 Results
The results of the analysis indicate a major radius (R0) ranging from 7.929 to 10.322 metres,
yielding an uncertainty of 2.393 metres. This interval encompasses the existing estimate of
9.0 metres for the major radius of the European H-mode DEMO baseline [95]. Nonetheless,
the analysis also suggests the potential for the DEMO to exceed the currently estimated size.
Results of the sensitivity analysis are summarised in Table 3.4. The major radius showed
the strongest dependence with H-factor, thermal 4He fraction, and plasma elongation, as
Figure 3.12 suggests. These results show that, of the uncertain parameters considered in
the study, these are those with the highest impact on the major radius uncertainty inside
PROCESS. Conversely, uncertainties in the operational divertor limit, core radius, and
tungsten impurity fraction exert minimal influence on the major radius uncertainty, as shown
in Figure 3.13.
Table 3.4 Results of the sensitivity analysis.
