Out of 6600 input samples analysed, 2868 were identified as feasible, while the remaining
3732 failed to meet the set design constraints in PROCESS. This discrepancy indicates
that certain input values did not return solutions satisfying the design requirements. As
depicted in Figure 3.14, plasma elongation and thermal 4He fraction are the most influential
parameters on the feasibility. Specifically, plasma elongation exhibits a distinct threshold
near 1.80, marked by a sharp rise in feasible solutions and a corresponding decline in
unfeasible ones. In contrast, thermal 4He fraction demonstrates a linear increase in feasibility.

