These findings suggest that maintaining plasma elongation at a minimum of 1.80 could
be crucial for satisfying the net electric power output constraint of 400 MW, while higher
concentrations of thermal 4He in the plasma appear beneficial for achieving the 2-hour pulse
length requirement. Supporting literature indicates that increased fusion power is associated

