Chapter 4
Optimisation under Uncertainty
Preface Part of the work contained in this chapter was presented at the IAEA International
Conference on Topical Issues in Nuclear Installation Safety (TIC) 2022: Strengthening
Safety of Evolutionary and Innovative Reactor Designs [192]. To appear in the corresponding
proceedings.
Neutronics simulations can be affected by two main sources of uncertainty: from the inherent
statistical uncertainty of Monte Carlo methods and from nuclear data uncertainty. While the
impact of the Monte Carlo uncertainty on the performance and safety assessments of nuclear
systems is generally considered, the impact of nuclear data uncertainty is often overlooked
since uncertainties in nuclear data are not always available, or these might be simplified to
reduce computational complexity. This chapter investigates the likelihood of nuclear data
uncertainty having consequences on neutronics optimisation problems, concluding that it
should be taken into account during the design activities of fusion reactors for finding safer
and better-performing designs. This chapter also explains how to perform reliability-based
design optimisation in fusion neutronics with nuclear data uncertainty in a computationally
efficient way.
4.1 Neutronics
Neutronics is the study of the motion and interactions of neutrons with matter. The neutron
transport equation balances the neutrons gained in the system with the neutrons lost by the

78 Optimisation under Uncertainty
system, and can be written as follows [193]:
1
