After determining the nuclide the neutron is colliding with, the next step is to determine
the type of reaction. The nuclide’s total microscopic cross-section is calculated as the sum
of all its possible reaction’s cross-sections σt = σe +σin +···+σf, where σe is the elastic
scattering cross-section, σin the inelastic scattering, σf fission, etc. Then, the reaction type is
calculated as:
