4.2.2 Reliability-based design optimisation
Reliability-based design optimisation (RBDO) attempts to find the design with the minimum
probability of failure, by wrapping the reliability analysis in an optimisation loop [74].
Considering that the model has a design variables vector θ , the output distribution is also
parameterised on this design vector fX(x;θ). The RBDO problem is thus
θ
∗ = arg minθ∈Θ
Z
