This work presents an extension for the Boolean operators allowing for uncertainty not
only in the inputs, but also in the dependence, which now can be specified for any interval
correlation ρ ⊆ [−1,1], having the Fréchet bounds as a special case when ρ = [−1,1].
Functions of Bernoulli random variables with uncertainty in dependence generally yield
interval probabilities, hence intervals may also be propagated through the derived operations.
5.2 Correlated AND as a copula
In this section it is argued that the above derived correlated AND is a bivariate copula
(2-copula) family, parameterised by a correlation coefficient ρ. Rewritten in a more standard
copula notation
