While non-decreasing is a necessary but not sufficient criteria for 2-increasing [238], Durante
and Jaworski [239] prove that C is a copula iff it satisfies criteria 1. and 2. and if the partial
derivatives are increasing (Corollary 2.4). That is, for every u ∈ [0,1],
