On the left of Figure 5.5 it is shown the probability of failure E1 for the interval scenario,
where the red area belongs to the independence case, blue to the mixed dependence case,
and green to the unknown dependence. It is possible to see how the uncertainty increases
as the dependence assumptions are relaxed from the Boolean operations. Intervals for the
probability of E1 are indicated in Table 5.5.

